Generative AI or Gen AI is already having a profound impact on open source software OSS development, sparking an explosion of AI-assisted contributions that raises urgent concerns about code volume, quality, and increasing burden on time-constrained maintainers.

42
00:04:44,192 --> 00:04:52,352
Despite these problematic trends, there are potential upsides, including increased productivity and bringing new contributors into the ecosystem.

43
00:04:52,526 --> 00:05:04,432
To provide robust empirical evidence to the evolving discussion about Gen AI and OSS, we developed, fielded, and analyzed a survey of 234 OSS contributors and maintainers.

44
00:05:04,672 --> 00:05:17,952
This research explores exactly how Gen AI is being deployed in OSS workflows, how it alters contribution dynamics, and how project leaders are navigating the complex intersection of new opportunities and emerging challenges.

45
00:05:18,112 --> 00:05:29,312
This is a great thing because this research provides some evidence about how one of the biggest transformations happening in software development is actually affecting open source communities and the function behind them.

46
00:05:29,486 --> 00:05:31,712
Finally, we get some real world data.

47
00:05:31,950 --> 00:05:37,632
Our findings indicate that the impact of generative AI on projects and workflows most often depends on the project scale.

48
00:05:37,902 --> 00:05:47,312
Larger projects were coordinated, maintainer teams currently bear the heaviest total administrative burden, which is quite interesting as these teams face surges in contribution volume.

49
00:05:47,566 --> 00:05:55,492
The larger the project, the more contributions, with large projects reporting that up to 31% of incoming contributions are low quality AI slop.

50
00:05:55,632 --> 00:05:59,312
